4. **Low — Direct GPU FPS / Heap Evaluation Blocked in Browser Sandbox**: `page.evaluate` is disabled in the browser subagent runner, so `1080p`/`1440p` quality tiers (`data-quality="high"` vs `"low"`, `2400×1350` & `3200×1800` DPR caps, and 20× enter/exit stress cycles) were verified via DOM/canvas bounds rather than raw `requestAnimationFrame` FPS numbers.

## 5. Next Steps for v0.4

1. **Host Lighthouse, Live FPS & Offline Service Worker Audit**: Run Lighthouse Desktop/Mobile, Chrome DevTools Performance FPS/Heap profiling (`1080p`/`1440p`/mobile), hardware trackpad `Ctrl+wheel` pinch test, and Chrome DevTools Offline reload across `/brain`, `/constellation`, and `/focus#microtasks`.
2. **Constellation Label De-confliction**: Add light label-offset / collision nudging in [computeDeterministicConstellationLayout](src/features/constellation/constellation.ts) when dense 20+ node graphs place text labels within the same horizontal band.
3. **R3F `<Html>` / Portal Unmount Polish**: Trace whether `@react-three/drei`'s `<Html>` label or toast portal caused the occasional `removeChild` notice during rapid panel/route teardown.
4. **Demo Data Microtask Showcase Toggle**: Optionally seed historical demo microtask runs (marked with `demo-` prefix) so `/experiments` with `reactionTime` can show a populated `>= 5` baseline vs intervention comparison immediately upon loading demo data.
</file>

